==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good combo potential. (Mainly because its C move has one of the highest fighting style stuns.)
* Fair for grinding.
* Excellent for PvP and bounty hunting due to its range, damage, and great [[Combos|combo]] potential.
* Fixes most of the things that makes [[Dark Step]] bad, such as larger range, bigger AoE, and faster moveset.
* Extra Requirement is easier to get compared to other V2 [[Fighting Styles|fighting styles]].
* All of the moves has a low startup lag.
*Beginner friendly V2 style.

|'''[Z] Rocket Kick'''
* Short cooldown.
* Great mobility.
* Decent knockback.
* Extremely hard to dodge without instinct due to its speed

|'''[X] Wind Bullet'''
* The small explosion has good [[AoE]].
* High speed.
* Instantaneous travel speed if directly aimed.
* Decent Range

|'''[C] Vermillion Drill'''
* Great stuns.
* High damage.

|'''[V] Maximum Overheat'''
* Extremely high damage with the fire tick damage (over time).
* The fire can [[Instinct/Break|break instinct]].
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Slow M1 speed.
* Hard to hit opponents from afar.
* Has semi-broken hitboxes when used with [[Buddha]], making its moves difficult to hit.
* Hard to aim in the air.

|'''[Z] Rocket Kick'''
* Can be dodged with [[Instinct]], unless it's a headshot.

|'''[X] Wind Bullet'''
* Hard to hit.
* Low range when compared to similar moves like [[Godhuman]] [X].
* Does not break [[Instinct]].

|'''[C] Vermillion Drill'''
* A bit hard to land in PvP if the players opponent is moving (The player has to be in the same area as their enemy is in).
* Can be dodged with [[Instinct]].

|'''[V] Maximum Overheat'''
* Highest mastery requirement in the game (400 Mastery).
* Long Cooldown.
* Can be interrupted.
}}
</tabber>

