==Tips & Tricks==
* Using Death Step with [[Ghoul]]'s V3 ability will allow the player to use Maximum Overheat infinitely. The player can simply activate Maximum Overheat, and when it runs out use [[Heightened Senses]] to be able to use the moves at 40% cooldown, then use Maximum Overheat again. And so, the player can maintain Maximum Overheat forever.
* With Heightened Senses, the player can activate Maximum Overheat even before the current Maximum Overheat Buff expires. Doing so resets the cooldown of Maximum Overheat, but the buff will still expire after a few seconds. Therefore, the player should wait until the Maximum Overheat Buff has fully ended before reactivating it.
* Death Step is recommended for killing [[Sea Beast]]s, as all skills can do damage to them. (Burning tick damage does not hit [[Sea Beast]]s)
* The user can use shiftlock + [[Flash Step]] to glitch inside the room, but [[Phoeyu, the Reformed|Phoeyu]] will say that the player is not prepared enough even if they meet the requirements until they use the [[Library Key|key]] to unlock the door.
** The user can also talk to [[Phoeyu, the Reformed|Phoeyu]] in [[Castle on the Sea]], but if they don't use the library key,  [[Phoeyu, the Reformed|Phoeyu]] will also say that the player is not prepared enough even if they get 400 mastery on dark step.
* The player can fly through thin walls with '''[Z] Rocket Kick''' which is still inconsistent.
* '''[C] Vermillion Drill''' links up well with '''[X] Wind Bullet''' and then '''[Z] Rocket Kick''' (or Z to X), allowing them to be easily used in a combo.

==Trivia==
* Death Step and its inferior version [[Dark Step]] are the only current fighting styles in the whole game that have a transformation-type move that enhances damage, as well as the only ones that have four moves.
* There is a bug where if '''[V] Maximum Overheat''' is active while switching fighting styles, the visual effect on the user's feet will stay until the user dies or leaves the game. This also applies to [[Dark Step]]. Keep in mind that this is purely visual effect, and does not provide any buffs.
* When using '''[Z] Rocket Kick''' on the edges of the volcano at the [[Magma Village]], the crater created will be purple, similar to [[T-Rex]]'s [F] move.
* The [V] ability Maximum Overheat has the highest mastery required for a move in the whole game, being 400 mastery, with other [V] moves usually having mastery requirements of 150, 225, 250, 300, 350 mastery. However, Maximum Overheat before [[Updates|Update 14]] used to have a mastery requirement of 450.
* Before [[Updates|Update 14]], Death Step's [V] was one of the most tedious things to get in the game, with things like [[Godhuman]], [[Sanguine Art]], [[Race Awakening]]s and others, did not exist at the time, so getting this move was one of the most tedious things to do at the time, similar to getting max level, 30m [[Bounty and Honor System|Bounty/Honor]], getting 600 mastery on something, owning the most expensive fruits, and others. But when [[Updates|Update 14]] rolled around, the mastery requirement went from 450 to 400.
* Death Step, along with [[Dark Step]], are the only fighting styles that have [V] abilities.
* Death Step's [V] move used to be called Devil Flames.

